message: "If you use this work, please cite it as below."
title: "The Effects of Airfoil Geometry on Lift-to-Drag Performance"
type: dataset
authors:
  - family-names: "Ravi"
    given-names: "Aarnav"
version: "1.0.0"
date-released: "2026-11-02"
license: MIT
keywords:
  - aerodynamics
  - airfoil
  - XFOIL
  - lift-to-drag ratio
  - NACA
  - Reynolds number
abstract: >-
  XFOIL study of how camber and thickness affect the maximum lift-to-drag
  ratio of five NACA 4-digit airfoils (0012, 2412, 4412, 0015, 0018) at
  Reynolds numbers from 100,000 to 1,000,000, validated against NACA
  Report 824 wind-tunnel data.
